{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhbvVu24gNEW7eYpAyj9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate, a refinement of the incumbent `iter0_candidate3`, and it passes the self-check. The check prints `OK` with a finite ELPD-LOO of -1023.4, about the same as the incumbent's -1023.0. That number comes from a short one-chain test fit, so it doesn't show whether the model beats the incumbent.\n\n**Name:** `asymmetric_alternation_representativeness`\n\n**Hypothesis:** People use the same local-representativeness score as the incumbent, with each person having their own decision sensitivity. The one change is how the score treats a sequence's alternation rate compared with the rate people expect:\n- **Too few alternations** (streaky, repetitive sequences) get the full penalty.\n- **Too many alternations**, up to perfect HTHT, get only a fraction of that penalty, set by one new fitted parameter `over_alt_ratio` (prior Beta(2,2)). Over-alternating is what people expect chance to look like.\n\nThis targets the critique's only finding that survives the false-discovery correction. The incumbent over-penalises perfect alternation: people chose the perfectly alternating sequence 76.8% of the time, against the model's predicted 85.8%.\n\n**What the check doesn't cover:**\n- **PSIS-LOO reliability:** the check warned that the ELPD-LOO estimate is unreliable on the test fit, with 11.1% of trials over the Pareto-k threshold against a 1% tolerance.\n- **Convergence and speed:** R-hat can't be computed from one chain, so convergence is unverified. Admission's full fit has to converge and finish each sampling run within 30 minutes.\n- **Novelty:** the check doesn't test whether the predictions differ enough from the incumbent's and the other live models'. If the fitted `over_alt_ratio` comes out near 1, they will be close.\n- **Periodicity penalty:** the incumbent's separate penalty for periodic sequences still applies to perfect alternation unchanged. So this change can only partly close the gap the critique found.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2391,"cache_read_input_tokens":56504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feffb9ad-1bb4-4223-ad13-491fe86d1ca9","uuid":"2d6766e9-2631-4dbf-ad6d-ed5e5b97280a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:37:18.066Z","request_id":"req_011CfhbvVJJWRsVTsZiSUAxM"}
